{
 "about": "Response classification (appendix A 3-5, 7, 54). Each case is one response as fetch.js returns it ({status, url, body, location}) for one operation of the ledger (op: the new row name; old_op: the current code's row, for the differential check). outcome is ok, or the exit code with its reason: transient (6, retry later), rate_limit (5, 30-minute block), login (4), noPost / owner_only / not_exist_blog / not_exist_post / blog_id_invalidate / not_exist_category (9), argument (2, a skill bug), drift (6, the response shape changed), query_restricted (8, whatever arrived is kept: kept counts the items). The order of the steps is the contract: a transport failure beats a block, a block beats a login wall, a login wall beats a missing target, a missing target beats a contract error, and a policy restriction is read only from an otherwise valid answer. All ids are synthetic. An outcome without a reason accepts any reason for that exit code.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "server-error-is-transient",
   "item": "4",
   "fact": "5xx is a transport failure: retry later, never a block.",
   "op": "post_list",
   "old_op": "post_list",
   "response": {
    "status": 502,
    "url": "https://m.blog.naver.com/api/blogs/sample_blog/post-list",
    "body": "<html>Bad Gateway</html>"
   },
   "outcome": {
    "code": 6,
    "reason": "transient"
   }
  },
  {
